<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">BP</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Anglo-Iranian Oil Company, Anglo-Persian Oil Company, British Petroleum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Persian Oil Company was a British company founded in 1909 to exploit oil discovered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masjed-soleyman">Masjed Soleyman</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> land. It built a refinery on Abadan island, leased from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazal-ibn-jabir">Sheikh Khazal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorramshahr">Mohammerah</a>, and the British government became its majority shareholder in 1914. Renamed the Anglo-Iranian Oil Company in 1935, it later became BP.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bp.jpg" alt="BP" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WhisperToMe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BPheadoffice.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
